;; The newest record in this log. UNSIGNED, on purpose.
;;
;; A tip that is stale, missing, or planted by whoever can write here costs a
;; resolution that fails or that lands on an older key set. It cannot
;; introduce a key: every record is still checked against its predecessor's
;; pre-rotation commitment and against the hash link (biscuit.rootkey/verify-log).
;; The same argument the packed block plane makes for its own unsigned tip
;; (ADR-2608170300) — what the pointer claims is re-checked downstream, so the
;; pointer is a hint rather than an authority.
;;
;; What a hostile tip CAN do is withhold: serve an old tip and hide a
;; rotation. That is a liveness failure, and a reader that cares compares
;; :seq against what it last saw.
